              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 3.7: Some integers and rational numbers on a number line"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.703,
            0.581,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Absolute value of a rational number"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.733,
            0.883,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "absolute value",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of a rational number "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "| x |"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , represents its distance from 0 on the number line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.775,
            0.731,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left| \\frac{5}{3} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}, \\left| -\\frac{5}{3} \\right|"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is also equal to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "| 0 | = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.825,
            0.886,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the absolute value of a positive number is the number itself. The absolute value of a negative number is its positive value. Therefore, the absolute value of any rational number is always non-negative, that is, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "| x | \\geq 0"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
